<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dora Riparia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dora Riparia is an Alpine river of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> that rises near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montgenevre-pass">Montgenèvre Pass</a> and flows east through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susa">Susa</a> Valley to join the Po at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a>. Its valley carried one of the main routes across the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> into the Po plain, used since antiquity. The ancient Taurini lived around its confluence with the Po.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dora-riparia.jpg" alt="Dora Riparia" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FRanco56 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dora_Riparia_a_Torino.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
